      <pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:00:07 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Nicole Noren spent 24 years at ESPN, much of that time producing award-winning investigative journalism on difficult topics, including human trafficking, sexual abuse, and concussions. But as ESPN embraced sports betting, Noren, in a new interview with Columbia Journalism Review, says the network repeatedly rejected her proposals to investigate gambling companies and addiction. The issue was personal: her grandfather, father, and a brother had all struggled with gambling addiction. So when ESPN</description>
